.TH CRAU-NBD 1 "September 2026" "crau-nbd 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
crau-nbd \- Linux Network Block Device server for CrAU v2 payload.bin images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crau-nbd
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B crau-nbd
is a high-performance Network Block Device daemon that allows read-only
block-level access to individual partitions (such as \fIsystem\fR, \fIvendor\fR,
or \fIboot\fR) stored inside Android or ChromeOS OTA \fBpayload.bin\fR images
without extracting the partition images to disk.
.PP
When passed an uncompressed (Stored) OTA \fB.zip\fR archive, \fBcrau-nbd\fR
automatically identifies the entry offset of \fBpayload.bin\fR and seeks
directly into the archive using zero-copy POSIX \fBpread\fR(2) calls.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBlist\fR \fIFILE\fR
Inspect the payload manifest, listing partition names, logical sizes, block counts,
and extent compression operation statistics.
.TP
\fBattach\fR \fB\-d\fR \fIDEV\fR \fB\-p\fR \fIPART\fR \fIFILE\fR
Attach the specified partition \fIPART\fR to the NBD block device node \fIDEV\fR.
.TP
\fBdetach\fR \fB\-d\fR \fIDEV\fR
Disconnect and release the specified NBD device.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-device\fR=\fIDEV\fR
Target Linux NBD block device node (e.g. \fI/dev/nbd0\fR).
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-partition\fR=\fINAME\fR
Name of the partition to map (e.g. \fIsystem\fR, \fIvendor\fR, \fIboot\fR).
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-cache-size\fR=\fIMB\fR
Size of the in-memory LRU block cache in megabytes. Default is 128 MB.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable detailed diagnostic and block I/O tracing.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display help summary and exit.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Output version information and exit.
.SH STANDARDS CONFORMANCE
This program conforms strictly to IEEE Std 1003.1 (POSIX.1) and the GNU Coding Standards.
